The '''Qiraash'''<ref name="By the Numbers">{{SWKidsYouTube|series=Star Wars By the Numbers|text=Every Alien Species in the Original Trilogy|video=yHVzcCGUM9U|nolive=1}}</ref> were a [[near-human]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] identifiable by their [[Color|pink]] skin and large craniums. [[Leesub Sirln]] was a Qiraash who was present at [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] shortly before the [[Battle of Yavin]].<ref name="A New Hope" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Qiraash_sketch.jpg|thumb|left|upright|An early production sketch of Leesub Sirln]]
The Qiraash first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']]. The first Qiraash to appear, Leesub Sirlin, was played by actress [[Pam Rose]].<ref name="Insider 154">{{InsiderCite|154|Bounty Hunters}}</ref> Originally identified only as "Weird Girl" in the production notes for [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], she was filmed in London as an extra for the cantina scene. She can be glimpsed briefly in the film just behind Kenobi and Skywalker in Chalmun's Cantina.<ref name="SW.com">{{SWArchive|url=episode-iv/bts/article/f20030502/index.html|text=Cantina Roll-Call: Shedding Light on Some Alien Aliases|int=Cantina Roll-Call: Shedding Light on Some Alien Aliases}}</ref> An early cut of the cantina sequence shows her more prominently, talking to [[Hrchek Kal Fas]] at the bar,<ref name="BTM">''[[Star Wars: Behind the Magic]]''</ref> and a production photo shows her standing in front of the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'', but these images were never part of the film.<ref name="SW.com" />

